    "renamed_note": "Raw string diff (before names have '@' already stripped; after names are the TS identifiers as written): 915/915 before-names have no exact-string match in after, and 231/231 after-names have no exact-string match in before -- essentially total churn, as expected for a kebab-case -> camelCase rewrite. Fuzzy pass: convert each removed before-name from kebab-case to camelCase (e.g. font-size-base -> fontSizeBase) and compare case-insensitively against every after-name (case-insensitive because v5 fully capitalizes size suffixes, e.g. control-padding-horizontal-sm -> controlPaddingHorizontalSm needs to match controlPaddingHorizontalSM). This finds 34 likely-renamed-not-removed tokens (border-radius-sm, control-padding-horizontal, control-padding-horizontal-sm, font-family, font-size-lg, font-size-sm, link-decoration, link-focus-decoration, link-hover-decoration, margin-lg, margin-md, margin-sm, margin-xs, padding-lg, padding-md, ...), all in the padding/margin/font-family/control-padding family where v4's per-scale suffix (-lg/-md/-sm/-xs) happens to survive a literal casing conversion. The remaining 881 removed names do not match any after-name even after normalization -- most are single-component variables (e.g. @btn-*, @table-*, @picker-*) that v5 replaced with component-level ComponentToken overrides (out of scope for this extraction, see interface.ts note) rather than global aliases, or use a reordered semantic ('primary-color' -> 'colorPrimary' swaps adjective-noun order, which a literal kebab->camel conversion cannot catch). This confirms the study's expectation: v4->v5 is a discontinuous architecture rewrite, not an incremental rename."
